# LiveMinutes secrets for the whole repo (every component reads this one file).
# Copy to .env in the repo root (gitignored, never commit it):  cp .env.example .env
# Format: KEY=value, no quotes, no spaces around "=". Other settings live in each component's settings.py.
# (Not the same as 1_ingestion/attendee/.env, which is Attendee's own config, generated in README section 1.4.)

# ---- 1. Ingestion ----

# Attendee API key, so the bridge and send_bot.sh can create bots, pause/resume them and post in chat.
# Easiest: ./make_account.sh you@example.com  (creates a login + key and writes it here)
# By hand: http://localhost:8000 -> log in -> API Keys -> Create API Key -> copy (shown only once).
ATTENDEE_API_KEY=

# Groq API key for Whisper speech-to-text (free tier is enough):
# https://console.groq.com/keys -> Create API Key -> copy (starts with gsk_).
# Groq blocks VPN / datacenter IPs (403 "Access denied"): turn your VPN off.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# The participants' live view (docs/UI.md). The bot posts <PUBLIC_BASE_URL>/m/<meeting> and an access code
# in the meeting chat once everyone has agreed. Empty = localhost (only the organizer's computer can open it).
# For a prototype: a free Cloudflare quick tunnel. `bash 1_ingestion/tunnel.sh` sets it while the bridge runs.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
# Optional: days the access code keeps working after the meeting ends (default 7).
# VIEW_ACCESS_DAYS=7

# ---- Live notes: the LLM summary and action items on the meeting page (1_ingestion/notes.py) ----
# Google Gemini, free tier: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey -> Create API key. The bridge sends the new transcript
# lines to it every 30 s. Empty: the meeting page shows sample data, labelled "Sample data", as before.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
LIVEMINUTES_LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
LIVEMINUTES_LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# Turn the live notes off (no LLM calls at all): LIVE_NOTES=0

# Or Anthropic (Claude) for the offline AMI runs (2_summarization/run.py --model llm): set the provider to anthropic
# and the key below (https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys, starts with sk-ant-; each call is billed). The bridge
# image doesn't include the Anthropic SDK, so the live notes in Docker need Gemini.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
